From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 16:21:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] libfetch: release the redirect URL on all paths in
 http_request()

Two leaks of the "new" URL:

 - A second Location header in the same reply released the previous
   allocation with free() rather than fetchFreeURL(), leaking new->doc.

 - Any error between parsing a Location header and consuming it at the
   bottom of the retry loop -- a malformed Content-Length, say --
   reaches the ouch label, which never released new at all.

Use fetchFreeURL() in the first case and release new at the ouch label
in the second.  The label is reached both before and after the loop
assigns new to url, so the release there is guarded against the alias.

Signed-off-by: Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@aeltra.eu>
---
 libfetch/http.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libfetch/http.c b/libfetch/http.c
index a08871f..ebc94c3 100644
--- a/libfetch/http.c
+++ b/libfetch/http.c
@@ -1028,7 +1028,7 @@ http_request(struct url *URL, const char *op, struct url_stat *us,
 				if (!HTTP_REDIRECT(conn->err))
 					break;
 				if (new)
-					free(new);
+					fetchFreeURL(new);
 				if (verbose)
 					fetch_info("%d redirect to %s", conn->err, p);
 				if (*p == '/')
@@ -1186,6 +1186,9 @@ http_request(struct url *URL, const char *op, struct url_stat *us,
 protocol_error:
 	http_seterr(HTTP_PROTOCOL_ERROR);
 ouch:
+	/* new aliases url once the retry loop has consumed a redirect */
+	if (new != NULL && new != url)
+		fetchFreeURL(new);
 	if (url != URL)
 		fetchFreeURL(url);
 	if (purl)
